# A reference catalog: the shape a project supplies, and the scope decision written as data rather than as prose.
#
# The compiler carries none of this. What a document may reach is the project's decision, and word.surf's answer
# is not the language's. Copy it, cut it down, and check it in, so a review can see the reachable surface change.
#
# The operator names are the real ones from mesh/deck/base/code/task/<scope>/make.ts, scope by scope. Three scopes
# are absent and each for its own reason, stated here because a reader will otherwise assume an oversight:
#
#   control   `walk` and `loop` would be a second spelling of the `walk` head, and `branch`, `switch`, `match`
#             and `pick` a second spelling of `fork`. Two spellings of one thing is the drift every rule here
#             exists to stop. `attempt` catches an error, and a document has nothing to catch.
#   random    `random` and `uuid` are not deterministic, so a document would render differently on the server and
#             in the browser, and differently on two reads, which breaks the content-addressed cache.
#   resource  `resolve` performs input and output, and the renderer does neither. That is what lets one compiled
#             component run on a server and in a browser.
#
# `now` is cut from `date` and `parse_json` from `type`, for the same two reasons in miniature: the first is not
# deterministic, and the second turns text into a shape nothing typed. The host passes the time in as a `host`
# parameter, which also makes a document testable.
#
# See note/term/view/04-catalog.md.

host deck, <reference>

list load
  <@view/text>
  <@view/hold>
  <@view/data>
  <@view/sound>
  <@view/media>
  <@view/turn>

list view
  <text/heading>
  <text/paragraph>
  <text/callout>
  <text/quote>
  <text/code>
  <text/gloss>
  <text/item>
  <text/list>
  <hold/grid>
  <hold/columns>
  <hold/block>
  <hold/box>
  <hold/divider>
  <hold/section>
  <data/table>
  <data/key-value>
  <data/timeline>
  <data/row>
  <sound/phoneme-chart>
  <sound/ipa-grid>
  <sound/script-sample>
  <sound/paradigm-table>
  <sound/minimal-pair>
  <sound/word-card>
  <media/image>
  <media/audio>
  <media/video>
  <media/figure>
  <turn/tabs>
  <turn/accordion>
  <turn/toggle>
  <turn/copy>
  <turn/link>
  <turn/when>

# string
list call
  <format>
  <join>
  <lowercase>
  <normalize>
  <pad-end>
  <pad-start>
  <replace>
  <scan>
  <split>
  <titlecase>
  <trim>
  <uppercase>
  <weld>
  # math
  <absolute>
  <add>
  <ceil>
  <clamp>
  <divide>
  <floor>
  <max>
  <mean>
  <min>
  <modulo>
  <multiply>
  <power>
  <root>
  <round>
  <subtract>
  <sum>
  # boolean
  <and>
  <eq>
  <gt>
  <gte>
  <lt>
  <lte>
  <ne>
  <negate>
  <or>
  # date, without `now`
  <diff>
  <format-date>
  <parse-date>
  <shift>
  # type, without `parse-json`
  <cast>
  <is>
  <to-boolean>
  <to-number>
  <to-string>
  # list, without the seven that take a callback. `keep`, `morph`, `find`, `locate` and `group` are evaluated
  # once per item against a sub-tree the author writes, and a document has no way to write one: `tree` is a
  # macro, not a function, and giving it a calling convention would be a second spelling of `walk` and `fork`.
  # An author filters by walking the list and forking inside it, which is the same power with the bound in the
  # head rather than in an operator's argument. `sort` and `dedupe` are cut with them because both are only
  # useful here with a key, and a key is a callback. See note/term/view/04-catalog.md.
  <chain>
  <count>
  <flatten>
  <nth>
  <pair>
  <reverse>
  <slice>

list task
  mesh
    host name, <select:language>
    host back, <one>
    list site
      mesh
        host name, <slug>
        list hold
          <is-equal>
        host sort, false
  mesh
    host name, <filter:phoneme>
    host back, <list>
    host size, 500
    list site
      mesh
        host name, <language>
        list hold
          <is-equal>
        host sort, false
      mesh
        host name, <kind>
        list hold
          <is-equal>
          <is-unequal>
        host sort, false
      mesh
        host name, <rank>
        list hold
          <is-equal>
          <is-above>
          <is-below>
        host sort, true
      mesh
        host name, <symbol>
        list hold
          <is-equal>
          <is-within>
        host sort, true
